        <ARI_SNOMED>11791001</ARI_SNOMED>
        <ARI_SurveyCode>NV</ARI_SurveyCode>
        <ARI_Version>2</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Vasculitis is an inflammation of blood vessels. When vasculitis is severe, blood cannot reach important organs or tissues. In severe cases, the tissue dies, which is called necrosis, and the term &quot;necrotizing vasculitis&quot; is used. It is also called &quot;systemic vasculitis&quot; since the severity of the disease can be widespread. 

Necrotizing vasculitis can lead to blood clots, weight loss, loss of weight, exhaustion, depression, fever, and widespread pain that worsens in the morning.
The specific location of vasculitis inflammation determines what tissue or organs (e.g., kidneys, fingers, head) are affected, and the type of vasculitis often depends on the location.  For more information, see the specific forms of vasculitis elsewhere on the website (listed above).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Necrotizing vasculitis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


