        <rdfs:comment>POEMS is an acronym that stands for the disorder&apos;s features, which may include Polyneuropathy (disease affecting many nerves), Organomegaly (abnormal enlargement of an organ), Endocrinopathy (diseases affecting certain hormone-producing glands that help to regulate sexual function), Monoclonal gammopathy and Skin Changes. POEMS syndrome is a rare blood disorder where there is an uncontrolled growth of a single clone of plasma cells, which results in abnormal accumulation of immunoglobulins in the blood.</rdfs:comment>
