        <ARI_UMLS>C0042164</ARI_UMLS>
        <ARI_Version>2.1</ARI_Version>
        <rdfs:comment>Uveitis is an inflammation of the uvea - a set of tissues that form a layer of eyeball that sits between the outer layers of the eye and the &quot;vitreous chamber&quot;, which forms the main body of the eye. The uvea itself has several kinds of tissue that can be affected by immune processes, all of which are called uveitis. About half of people who receive a diagnosis of uveitis have an autoimmune form of the disease. Uveitis is a term that means &quot;inflammation of the uvea&quot;, and not all forms of uveitis are autoimmune, and not all individuals diagnosed with uveitis have an autoimmune form of uveitis. 

The most common form of autoimmune uveitis is intermediate uveitis.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Uveitis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


