        <rdfs:comment>Vogt-Koyanagi-Harada (VKH), is a rare disease that affects multiple systems including the nervous system and skin. The disease results in rapid vision loss as well as loss of hearing and hair. Although the cause of VKH is unknown, researchers believe that it is an immune response to a genetic defect of the Human Leukocyte antigen (HLA). Other researchers believe that there may be a genetic predisposition for VKH and may only be expressed by an environmental trigger.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Vogt-Koyanagi-Harada disease</rdfs:label>
